{"id": "EUVD-2026-97658", "enisaUuid": "e9bd02dd-4937-3515-a361-6ab4644e0d25", "description": "LibreNMS before 26.9.0 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in PortsController::purge that allows global-read users to physically delete ports without delete privileges. Attackers with read-only accounts can send DELETE requests to /ports/purge, using purge=all to irreversibly erase every deleted port on all visible devices.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T16:05:37", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/librenms/librenms/security/advisories/GHSA-9qcg-rgg9-mpjg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/librenms-before-26.9.0-missing-authorization-in-port-purge-via-portscontroller"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h6hv-5g7p-j2pv", "CVE-2026-109356"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14a8984a-a7da-3cbf-8479-71eb350e966a", "product": {"name": "librenms", "vendor": {"name": "librenms"}}, "product_version": "0 <26.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e3e578bc-264e-3a46-9196-46c30f516738", "vendor": {"name": "librenms"}}], "isExploited": false}